WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.250 --> 00:00:01.890
- Hi there, I'm Jennifer Garner

00:00:01.890 --> 00:00:04.610
and I'm going to take a
BuzzFeed quiz to find out

00:00:04.610 --> 00:00:07.560
which Jennifer Garner character I am.

00:00:07.993 --> 00:00:11.160
(light-hearted music)

00:00:13.480 --> 00:00:15.330
First, choose a Hollywood hunk:

00:00:15.410 --> 00:00:18.160
Ryan Gosling, Henry Golding, great.

00:00:18.410 --> 00:00:19.810
Mark Ruffalo, hm.

00:00:20.020 --> 00:00:22.670
Josh Duhamel, Matthew
McConaughey, Will Smith.

00:00:23.660 --> 00:00:24.493
Ideal.

00:00:24.666 --> 00:00:26.115
(sputters)

00:00:26.115 --> 00:00:27.840
How do you choose one of these guys?

00:00:27.840 --> 00:00:30.280
I mean it's hard not to choose
one of them that I know.

00:00:30.280 --> 00:00:32.540
Matthew I've worked with
twice so he wins, bink.

00:00:32.540 --> 00:00:35.290
Next, pick your favorite movie genre:

00:00:35.690 --> 00:00:36.650
horror, no.

00:00:36.860 --> 00:00:37.693
Action.

00:00:38.010 --> 00:00:40.740
I'm in an action film
and I do like this film

00:00:40.740 --> 00:00:43.660
but typically I get too
stressed out, no thank you.

00:00:43.720 --> 00:00:45.080
Romcom, yes.

00:00:45.090 --> 00:00:46.380
Sci-fi, no.

00:00:46.600 --> 00:00:47.700
Fantasy, meh.

00:00:47.780 --> 00:00:48.910
Comedy, yes.

00:00:48.950 --> 00:00:50.130
Romcom or comedy?

00:00:50.378 --> 00:00:52.332
(clicks tongue)

00:00:52.332 --> 00:00:53.310
I'm gonna have to go romcom.

00:00:53.310 --> 00:00:55.080
Now choose your favorite favorite

00:00:55.080 --> 00:00:56.960
Jennifer Garner red carpet look.

00:00:57.370 --> 00:00:58.203
That's horrifying.

00:00:58.203 --> 00:01:00.080
The 60th Golden Globes.

00:01:00.380 --> 00:01:02.910
Wow, we were really going for period look

00:01:02.920 --> 00:01:04.430
with the hair over the ears.

00:01:04.520 --> 00:01:07.600
The 54th Emmy Awards,
that was Ralph Lauren.

00:01:07.890 --> 00:01:08.723
That was pretty,

00:01:08.723 --> 00:01:10.880
and that dress didn't come
together until that day.

00:01:10.880 --> 00:01:12.530
75th Academy Awards.

00:01:12.690 --> 00:01:13.860
Definitely not her.

00:01:14.050 --> 00:01:15.870
The 80th Academy Awards.

00:01:16.034 --> 00:01:18.500
(sighs) The long bang.

00:01:18.780 --> 00:01:19.613
That's one of my favs.

00:01:19.613 --> 00:01:23.610
88th Academy Awards, that's Versace,

00:01:23.610 --> 00:01:25.270
and the 90th Academy Awards.

00:01:25.270 --> 00:01:27.370
Whoa that blue dress was very blue.

00:01:27.580 --> 00:01:28.870
Which one is the most me?

00:01:30.490 --> 00:01:33.700
I really loved the hair
and the drama of this one.

00:01:34.890 --> 00:01:35.723
Take that.

00:01:35.723 --> 00:01:38.090
Pick your go-to movie theater snack.

00:01:38.690 --> 00:01:39.523
Wine.

00:01:39.698 --> 00:01:40.680
(chuckles) That was easy.

00:01:40.680 --> 00:01:43.030
Choose a punny name for your pet chicken.

00:01:43.120 --> 00:01:44.180
Mother Clucker.

00:01:44.380 --> 00:01:45.900
That's good.

00:01:45.950 --> 00:01:47.500
Dixie Chick, Princess Lay-a.

00:01:48.140 --> 00:01:49.260
These are very good.

00:01:49.690 --> 00:01:51.200
Gretch-hen Wiener.

00:01:51.370 --> 00:01:52.240
I'm not gonna lie,

00:01:52.240 --> 00:01:54.390
this is the toughest
one we've come across.

00:01:54.480 --> 00:01:56.100
Goldie Hen, hm.

00:01:56.380 --> 00:01:57.213
Princess Lay-a.

00:01:58.270 --> 00:01:59.103
I'm Jenna Rink.

00:02:00.075 --> 00:02:03.010
(laughs) I could have told
you that without doing this.

00:02:03.030 --> 00:02:05.810
The person that I am closest
to is Jenna Rink, yes.

00:02:06.030 --> 00:02:08.580
I'm 30 (chuckling), flirty and thriving.

00:02:08.970 --> 00:02:10.050
Plus 16 years.

00:02:10.910 --> 00:02:13.510
Whether you're closer in age to 30 or 13,

00:02:13.550 --> 00:02:16.630
or the two combined, you are the lovable

00:02:16.630 --> 00:02:18.140
and self-determined Jenna Rink.

00:02:18.140 --> 00:02:20.920
People tend to be attracted
to your vibrant personality

00:02:20.920 --> 00:02:22.280
and infectious presence.

00:02:22.300 --> 00:02:23.450
And who can blame them?

00:02:23.570 --> 00:02:25.400
You're the life of the
party in any setting.

00:02:25.400 --> 00:02:27.820
With or without whipping out
the Thriller choreography.

00:02:27.820 --> 00:02:28.820
I still know Thriller.

00:02:28.820 --> 00:02:30.710
Though you have a tendency to wanna fit in

00:02:30.710 --> 00:02:31.570
with the cool crowd,

00:02:31.570 --> 00:02:33.220
I don't think that is true about me,

00:02:33.220 --> 00:02:34.380
just that specific thing,

00:02:34.380 --> 00:02:35.930
I'm not very good at the cool crowd.

00:02:35.930 --> 00:02:38.820
You never stray too far away
from your authentic self.

00:02:38.860 --> 00:02:41.240
I almost forgot, you're
flirty and thriving.

00:02:41.608 --> 00:02:42.890
(clicks tongue) Flirty, thriving.

00:02:43.300 --> 00:02:44.410
Yeah, I would agree with that.

00:02:44.410 --> 00:02:47.060
I think I'm probably of all the
characters I've ever played,

00:02:47.060 --> 00:02:48.658
I'm probably most like that chick.

00:02:48.658 --> 00:02:51.825
(light-hearted music)

